{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793765996456827002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"soldierly-arbitrary-hackee","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":2},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793765960875058001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c93142eb-2df1-4b7c-9d52-682c39af1821","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"772b-3517-9301-4db3"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n4 compaction tests drop the integer exit code of the in-process `compact_all_cli` call and then assert only absences, so they pass when compaction does nothing and fails.\n\nObserved 2026-11-03 at `2e8e8051796` (session a85e3cd3, while working depressant-existent-squirrel): a scratch-only pytest plugin replaced `rebar._commands.compact.compact_all_cli` and `compact_cli` with a function that returns 1 without doing anything. All 4 tests below still PASSED (`4 passed in 77.35s`):\n\n- `tests/unit/test_compact_sweep_perf.py::test_no_history_walk_runs_while_the_store_lock_is_held`: the only assertion is `assert not walks_under_lock`.\n- `tests/unit/test_compact_sweep_perf.py::test_the_sweep_yields_when_a_writer_takes_the_lock_mid_run`: the only assertion is `len(snapshotted) <= 1`, which 0 folds satisfies.\n- `tests/unit/test_compact_all_selection.py::test_dry_run_never_pushes`: the only assertion is `assert not calls`.\n- `tests/unit/test_compact_all_selection.py::test_no_commit_never_pushes`: the only assertion is `assert not calls`.\n\nThe sibling tests in `tests/unit/test_compact_fold_prelock.py` already guard against this with an `ANCHOR:` assertion (for example `assert seen, \"ANCHOR: ...\"`) or a SNAPSHOT precondition. In the same plugin run, those tests were not separated out, so their behavior under the seeded failure has not been measured.\n\nNot checked: `tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_push_pending.py:97` drops the `_cli.main([\"store\", \"fsck\"])` result and asserts only `\"PUSH_PENDING\" not in out`. That shape is the same, but it is unmeasured.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Each of the 4 tests asserts `compact_all_cli(...) == 0` and an anchor showing the sweep reached the code under test (for the 2 sweep-perf tests, at least 1 SNAPSHOT or 1 recorded walk; for the 2 selection tests, the expected early-return or no-commit path ran), so the seeded no-op-returning-1 plugin makes each one FAIL.\n- [ ] The fsck_push_pending site is measured under a seeded fsck failure and either strengthened the same way or recorded on this ticket as not vacuous.\n- [ ] The touched test files pass under `pytest`.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"83ba-5be6-dad3-43ec","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Compaction sweep tests pass when the sweep fails","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0d07122f-8ab9-48ef-903f-262e5d0cc95c","c93142eb-2df1-4b7c-9d52-682c39af1821"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793765996456827002,"uuid":"b648cab5-77bc-4003-8b46-9795d4295468"}